{"id": "SGU_Episode_298", "title": "SGU Episode 298", "type": "structured", "description": "The Skeptic's Guide to the Universe, Episode 298 Transcript", "metadata": {"title": "SGU Episode 298", "date": "March 30 2024", "year": 2024, "month": 3, "day": 30, "rogues": ["Rebecca Watson", "Steven Novella", "Jay Novella", "Evan Bernstein", "Bob Novella"], "quotee_url": "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brian_Caplan", "quote": "\n There are two sources of error: Either you lack sufficient data, or you fail to take advantage of the data that you have. \n", "quotee": "\n Brian Caplan \n", "quotee_title": "", "guests": [{"guest": "Kenny Feder", "guest_title": "", "guest_url": "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kenny_Feder"}], "categories": [], "podcast_url": "https://www.theskepticsguide.org/podcasts/episode-298", "episode_number": 298}, "sections": [{"id": 0, "text": "You're listening to the Skeptics' Guide to the Universe, your escape to reality.\n", "title": "Introduction", "metadata": {"title": "Introduction"}, "sections": [{"id": 1, "text": "Hello and welcome to the Skeptic's Guide to the Universe, today is Tuesday, March 30th 2011, and this is your host Steven Novella.  Joining me this week are Bob Novella.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}, {"id": 2, "text": "Hey everybody.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "B", "speaker": "Bob Novella"}}, {"id": 3, "text": "Rebecca Watson.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}, {"id": 4, "text": "Hello everyone.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "R", "speaker": "Rebecca Watson"}}, {"id": 5, "text": "Jay Novella.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}, {"id": 6, "text": "Hey guys.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "J", "speaker": "Jay Novella"}}, {"id": 7, "text": "And Evan Bernstein.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}, {"id": 8, "text": "Hi everyone.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "E", "speaker": "Evan Bernstein"}}, {"id": 9, "text": "Evan, what happened today?", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "J", "speaker": "Jay Novella"}}, {"id": 10, "text": "You mean today, April 2nd, on this day in history?", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "E", "speaker": "Evan Bernstein"}}]}, {"id": 11, "text": "", "title": "This Day in Skepticism", "metadata": {"timestamp": "April 2, 1845", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "This Day in Skepticism"}, "sections": [{"id": 12, "text": "1845, the first surviving daguerrotype photograph showing details of the sun was taken by two french physicists.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "E", "speaker": "Evan Bernstein"}}, {"id": 13, "text": "Both of whom went blind shortly after.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "R", "speaker": "Rebecca Watson"}}, {"id": 14, "text": "They didn't realize that actually looking at it through a device will make you blind.", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "E", "speaker": "Evan Bernstein"}}]}, {"id": 15, "text": "", "title": "News Items", "metadata": {"title": "News Items"}, "sections": [{"id": 16, "text": "", "title": "Item 1", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "Item 1"}, "sections": []}]}, {"id": 17, "text": "", "title": "Who's That Noisy?", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "Who's That Noisy?"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 18, "text": "", "title": "Questions and Emails", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "Questions and Emails"}, "sections": [{"id": 19, "text": "", "title": "Question 1", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "Question 1"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 20, "text": "", "title": "Question 2", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "Question 2"}, "sections": []}]}, {"id": 21, "text": "", "title": "Interview with \"...\"", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "Interview with \"...\""}, "sections": []}, {"id": 22, "text": "", "title": "Science or Fiction", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "Science or Fiction"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 23, "text": "", "title": "Skeptical Quote of the Week", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "Skeptical Quote of the Week"}, "sections": [{"id": 24, "text": "", "metadata": {"speaker": "<unknown>"}}]}, {"id": 25, "text": "", "title": "Announcements", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "Announcements"}, "sections": [{"id": 26, "text": "The Skeptics' Guide to the Universe is produced by SGU Productions, dedicated to promoting science and critical thinking. For more information on this and other episodes, please visit our website at theskepticsguide.org, where you will find the show notes as well as links to our blogs, videos, online forum, and other content. You can send us feedback or questions to info@theskepticsguide.org. Also, please consider supporting the SGU by visiting the store page on our website, where you will find merchandise, premium content, and subscription information. Our listeners are what make SGU possible.", "metadata": {"links": ["http://www.theskepticsguide.org", "https://www.theskepticsguide.org/shop"], "speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}]}, {"id": 27, "text": "", "title": "References", "metadata": {"title": "References"}, "sections": []}]}